{
  "messages": [
    {
      "docs": "Create `instance(id)` from a bootstrap matching `checkpoint`, and open the job that adopts\nits committee. `bootstrap`: `CompactBootstrap` encoding.",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "config",
          "type": {
            "defined": "Config"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "checkpoint",
          "type": {
            "array": [
              "u8",
              32
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "bootstrap",
          "type": {
            "vec": "u8"
          }
        }
      ],
      "name": "Init",
      "tag": 0
    },
    {
      "docs": "Step 1 of an update, at `instance(id)`: `update` is a `CompactUpdate` encoding, `signers`\na `SignerWitness` encoding. Opens `job(id, job_id)`. The update is in the store's layout,\nor in the layout of a later fork of the instance's schedule that its attested header has\nreached: the job then starts from the store upgraded to that layout, and applying it\nupgrades the instance's store.",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "update",
          "type": {
            "vec": "u8"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "signers",
          "type": {
            "vec": "u8"
          }
        }
      ],
      "name": "Open",
      "tag": 1
    },
    {
      "docs": "Step 2, at the job: the Miller loops.",
      "name": "Miller",
      "tag": 2
    },
    {
      "docs": "One part of the job's committee adoption: `n / parts` uncompressed keys.",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "part",
          "type": "u8"
        },
        {
          "name": "keys",
          "type": {
            "vec": {
              "array": [
                "u8",
                96
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "name": "Adopt",
      "tag": 3
    },
    {
      "docs": "Step 3, at the job: the final exponentiation, then `Apply` to the instance.",
      "name": "Finish",
      "tag": 4
    },
    {
      "docs": "Reply with this actor's state (`StateReply`), the read idiom of LEZ v0.4.",
      "name": "Read",
      "tag": 5
    },
    {
      "docs": "As `Read`, carrying bytes the program ignores: for measuring what a message byte costs\n(`lez/RESULTS.md`, \"What the LEZ v0.4 shell costs\").",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "padding",
          "type": {
            "vec": "u8"
          }
        }
      ],
      "name": "ReadPadded",
      "tag": 6
    },
    {
      "docs": "At `header(id, slot)`: prove the facts of `request` under this record and reply to the\ncaller with an [`attest::Attestation`] (their statement identifiers and values), or refuse\nwith a code. Sent as the root of a transaction, with nobody to reply to, the statement\nidentifiers are emitted as an event ([`ATTESTED_SELECTOR`]). Changes no state.",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "request",
          "type": {
            "defined": "Request"
          }
        }
      ],
      "name": "Attest",
      "tag": 7
    },
    {
      "docs": "The private placement (Stage 2): the whole verification of one update in one call, at any\nactor of this program (meant to run privately). `store` is the instance's `CompactStore`\nencoding; `adoption` the committee's keys when the update adopts one. Sends\n`ApplyVerified` to `instance(id)`.",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "config",
          "type": {
            "defined": "Config"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "checkpoint",
          "type": {
            "array": [
              "u8",
              32
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "store",
          "type": {
            "vec": "u8"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "update",
          "type": {
            "vec": "u8"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "signers",
          "type": {
            "vec": "u8"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "adoption",
          "type": {
            "vec": {
              "array": [
                "u8",
                96
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "name": "VerifyAll",
      "tag": 8
    },
    {
      "docs": "`instance(id)` → `job(id, job_id)`: the job step 1 produced (`Job` encoding).",
      "fields": [
